# Odoo Python

Follow conventions in `.github/copilot-instructions.md` and existing repo code.

## Style & Linting

- **Ruff**: formatting + linting, line length 88, sorted imports (stdlib → third-party → Odoo → relative).
- **Translations**: `self.env._("text")` in model methods (not bare `_()`). Lazy form: `self.env._("text %s", value)`. When adding/changing/removing these strings, update `bonuscard_odoo/i18n/sv_SE.po` in the same change (see Translation Maintenance Rule in `.github/copilot-instructions.md`).
- **Pylint**: must pass `.pylintrc-mandatory`. Avoid `# noqa` / pylint disables unless justified.
- **XML** (in Python-adjacent changes): all `<record>` tags need `id`; pass `oca-checks-odoo-module`.

## Odoo 19 Specifics

- `res.partner` has `phone` only — no `mobile` field.
- Security: `res.groups` membership via `user_ids`; default memberships in `noupdate="1"` data.

## Testing

- Mock HTTP — cover HTTP failures and API-level business errors in payload.
- Manual integration tests: tag `bonuscard_integration`, exclude from CI defaults.
- Patch Odoo model methods by **import path string**, not `patch.object`:

```python
# ✅ GOOD
patch("odoo.addons.bonuscard_odoo.models.bonuscard_api_service.BonuscardApiService.method", ...)

# ❌ BAD — Odoo model attrs are read-only
patch.object(model_instance, "method", ...)
```

## New Capabilities

Add fields, views, security, and tests together. Prefer root-cause fixes over view-only patches.
